{"title":"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Note:\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note:</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be real numbers satisfying\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/9/8c9c8a3e2c9027abba620c84789f4c9f7586f6cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1 + x_2 + \\dots + x_n = 0, \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x_1^2 + x_2^2 + \\dots + x_n^2 = 1.\\]\" width=\"423\" height=\"19\" />\nFor each subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27c953b6706f81ab1e46b6e765d03937e0c30f9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\subseteq \\{1, 2, \\dots, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />, define\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/45717db127bc90fec3df2da18ec709f9df5a8619.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_A = \\sum_{i \\in A} x_i.\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"39\" />\n(If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the empty set, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04abe8df443b3c5da24ba78c54b124ff7b9a8c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_A = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />.)\n</p><p>Prove that for any positive number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" />, the number of sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3ad4e2fdd660d35b316cbd593ecd899c1de5367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_A \\ge \\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/e/e7e289647937359a45ec83caaba588171b6773f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n - 3}/\\lambda^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" />.  For what choices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> does equality hold?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For convenience, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e26a068fc84477720d7f4b374e42dcb57c80fd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=\\{1,2,\\dots,n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7be1f3117898e0b6c56481acdc40186ee6d1fc7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j\\leq n} x_ix_j=\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{n}x_i\\right)^2-\\left(\\sum_{j=1}^{n} x_i^2\\right)=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"353\" height=\"57\" />, so the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> taken two at a time is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/0/9c0935f19767bef282a174dea1c15011e246720b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />. Now consider the following sum:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bd60549eb1a64850064dff032d1168ace76fa90.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{A\\subseteq N}S_A^2=2^{n-1}\\left(\\sum_{j=1}^{n} x_i^2\\right)+2^{n-1}\\left(\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j\\leq n} x_ix_j\\right)=2^{n-2}.\\]\" width=\"438\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856a224d483ed0bed914dd06c304cdc4ede48643.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_A^2\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"19\" />, it follows that at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c9705db9ebe275308d9a8d884116ec06db0f9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n-2}/\\lambda^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" /> sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bce21b0152365260c37c35e28759cce244616f35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\subseteq N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/d/ffda14f08b69c0d4659fe4bde19e9e44bc12ad2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_A|\\geq \\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a300051ee47ee79833011a007fbfb5c71e90bdb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_A+S_{N/A}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />. It follows that at most half of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b521125dee0cf0ad97dc4e77d84073d8644984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/895dfc7766c97f444ac753b50a6ebef640b0f8b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_A|\\geq\\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> are positive. This shows that at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a15e0ad06642ebb510eb90d81ae8a51dccecc899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n-3}/\\lambda^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"21\" /> sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bce21b0152365260c37c35e28759cce244616f35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\subseteq N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/6/3b686510bf93bce6fe2b196bf46a6fa70a043ee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_A\\geq \\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Note that if equality holds, every subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b55d8e82f5787a1f1213a7957a695f66bf23a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_A\\in\\{-\\lambda,0,\\lambda\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />. It immediately follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/a/77a8c20dc7d40f35bd99fa32cd43291c6e386ba4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,x_2,\\ldots , x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" /> is a permutation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/0/6c0eb32d64def567e870463fd441cc429743a879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\lambda,-\\lambda,0,0,\\ldots , 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />. Since we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e426330745b2bb5b009cb02a1f2d46833b276b2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"79\" height=\"48\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/f/cbfd62aff9aa81f588796e2b8980bb74328f0df2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda=1/\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/3/1a3da6aeeb160f3fd6772c3f06d01b8727ba387d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i=x_1,x_2,...,x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"13\" /> It is evident that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c81295d171fdfd767bd8840f3a97f99c8e7d0a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i = \\frac{(-1)^i}{\\sqrt{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"89\" height=\"45\" /> for evens because of the second equation and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2c179aacd38a5d2a303f3b50d2ea8cc4b0d2c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i=\\frac{(-1)^i}{\\sqrt{n-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"103\" height=\"45\" /> for odds(one term will be 0 to maintain the first condition). \nWe may then try and get an expression for the maximum number of sets that satisfy this which occur when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26a7294d60b34975b35b44b4fcd446cbfda3353c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"67\" height=\"43\" />:\nsince it will be \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/f/fcf4c068990a47c6d0c1c208b7e05dfedf094fc3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_1 + x_2 + ... + x_n\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"13\" />\nfor any choice of A we pick, it will have to be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93fdb245584f75768bb73b7ceca409c2cc0d6b5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"28\" height=\"41\" /> which means we can either pick 0 negative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fcaeea91c5bea53f0f7fb9dc6300816e6320b58f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/1233d0dcd103cc6ee1353e914244e3d66573a39e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> negatives for j positive terms. Since we also have that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f275b1f33e3c37ece0e41964f0bcb806e95b46b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" /> positive and negative terms for evens. Which then gives us:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bd4581df75d857e75ad5bda70aba24285fb41a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{k}\\sum_{i=0}^{k-1} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{i}\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"55\" />\nand \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc2af35f5b8d6b68821d6eb267bb16d2ced17f40.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{\\frac{n}{2}}\\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{k}\\left(2^{\\frac{n}{2}} - \\sum_{i=k}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{i}\\right)\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"64\" />\nFor odd values, let it be the same as the last even valued sequence where n is even(i.e. the same as the sequence before it but with an extra 0 in one of the spots). Then, the following is apparent: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/8/db89716e9424a42d28b479a422cab529da178b5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{\\lfloor\\frac{n}{2}\\rfloor}\\binom{\\lfloor \\frac{n}{2}\\rfloor}{k}\\left(2^{\\lfloor\\frac{n}{2}\\rfloor} - \\sum_{i=k}^{\\lfloor\\frac{n}{2}\\rfloor}\\binom{\\lfloor \\frac{n}{2}\\rfloor}{i}\\right)  \\le n2^{n-3}\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"64\" />\nThus, we may say that this holds to be true for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ecfb85d70b699dcb32cdf127914f410f91c561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n2^{n-3}$\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> grows faster than the sum. Note that equality holds when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8f63436338889956d3430fcb6bc63dcfdf0b4a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_A \\in \\{\\lambda,0,-\\lambda\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" /> for all i which occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/279276a745c609c791241d483edc46043840a04b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},0,....$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"166\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c19f9949a968c089484703b90b3bd2d0c1802cf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"61\" height=\"41\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2ef0f098c0ad268ddcd038fac32be5501996ca8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_A=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"76\" height=\"43\" /> is the only choice for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3ad4e2fdd660d35b316cbd593ecd899c1de5367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_A \\ge \\lambda$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note:\">Note:</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Note:\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The proof to the last inequality is as follows:\nFirst we may rewrite this as being:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/28255e459022e02f21919241b98ac67eb7b057cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{k} \\left( 2^{\\frac{n}{2}} - \\sum_{i=k}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{i}\\right)  \\le n2^{n-3}\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"64\" />\nThus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f3079a3fcad3f1e01f157366d9a6d27b7f9a3fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^n - 2^{\\frac{n}{2}} - \\sum_{k=1}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{k} \\sum_{i=k}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{i} \\le n2^{n-3}\\]\" width=\"293\" height=\"55\" />\n(the second equation is because the sum of the binomial coefficient is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/d/a4d57128245be2d444f6246f98d51610e38f63a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{\\frac{n}{2}} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"19\" />)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8ad1a592ec78f10fc4a9c502e5c28e14d7d35d2b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^n - 2^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\le n2^{n-3} + \\sum_{k=1}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{k} \\sum_{i=k}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{i}\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"55\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/adda28ad08ae845932a7a21a20789ff810407774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n - 2^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\le n2^{n-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf8265616aa5992dee93307d9f145357b7796f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf614a4e6f027b029d26a49bb50ced1b9262fd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{k} \\sum_{i=k}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{i} \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"176\" height=\"59\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, it is apparent that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd111f3c38334b62151abcf66712687546d3484d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{k} \\sum_{i=0}^{k-1} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{i} \\le n2^{n-3}\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"55\" />\nmust be true for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf8265616aa5992dee93307d9f145357b7796f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />(because if we rewrite this we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/6/ff6967bee178214a171793af1dac4c533ef0957d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{\\frac{n}{2}}\\left(8-n\\right) \\le 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"22\" />.) For all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2c7bb4aad88ca1d5289e4469389120e9296914e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\le n &lt; 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> however, we may use some logic to first layout a plan. Since for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/2464d45a4483ad4cf4246f65f047bbb449f13bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=6,n=4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/5/1b5d5db7391fa92ef5f65fc505927a4b086380c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n} - 2^{\\frac{n}{2}} = n2^{n-3} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"165\" height=\"19\" />, we may say that whole sum will be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ecfb85d70b699dcb32cdf127914f410f91c561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n2^{n-3}$\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/9/6c99e664ae339db5e772b153118306baf1bdaa62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{k} \\sum_{i=k}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{i} \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"176\" height=\"59\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> Plugging this inequality back in gives us:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/125a31e0f6786d79587616dea8e526e2e22d96f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{n} - 2^{\\frac{n}{2}} - \\sum_{k=1}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{k} \\sum_{i=k}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{i} \\le 2^{n} - 2^{\\frac{n}{2}} - 1 = n2^{n-3}\\]\" width=\"410\" height=\"55\" /> \nbecause of the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/6/1b6cd8ea6af5827d3f58a1ce590dc4502232e7e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$- \\sum_{k=1}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{k} \\sum_{i=k}^{\\frac{n}{2}} \\binom{\\frac{n}{2}}{i} \\le -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"208\" height=\"59\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\">USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO\" title=\"2012 USAMO\">2012 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\"><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017010206\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.064 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 458/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1261/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 54/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16227/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.117      1 -total\n 57.59%    6.978      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 40.37%    4.892      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11058:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 202610